Yalb
The browser you own, not the one that owns you.
Yalb is an open-source, privacy-first desktop browser for Windows, built with C# WinForms and Microsoft Edge WebView2. It is keyboard-driven, telemetry-free, and designed to be forked, hacked, and remixed by anyone.
Because Yalb is open source, anyone can change the code, add onto it, and build their own version. For those who don't want to — or don't know how to — edit and build the code themselves, we publish ready-to-use flavors.
🧬 The Yalb Family
Table
Flavor	Description
Maeger	Minimal. Fast. No distractions. The stripped-down experience.
Main	The balanced everyday driver — a thoughtful mix of all features.
Segfault	Nightly build. Bleeding edge. Preview and pre-release channel.
Daemon	The kitchen sink. Every option from every version, all at once.
Onion	Privacy-focused. Built for people who take their anonymity seriously.
Dev	Built for developers. Tools, integrations, and workflows that actually help.
Note: Maeger is the first public pre-release. More flavors are coming soon.
🚀 Quick Start
Download a Pre-built Flavor
Go to Releases.
Download the ZIP for the flavor you want (e.g., Yalb.Maeger-vX.X.X.zip).
Extract it anywhere.
Double-click the .exe.
Requirements: Windows 10 (1709+) or Windows 11 (x64). WebView2 Runtime is pre-installed on Windows 11; Windows 10 users may need the Evergreen Bootstrapper.
🛠️ Building from Source
Prerequisites
.NET 8 SDK
Node.js (for the startpage)
pnpm
Windows 10/11 with WebView2 Runtime
Clone the Repository
bash
git clone https://github.com/Initial-Mozartt/Yalb.git
cd Yalb
Build the Startpage
The browser uses a local startpage server. You need to build it first.
bash
cd Yas
pnpm install --filter @workspace/startpage
pnpm --filter @workspace/startpage run build
If the build fails, try again. If it still fails, clean and rebuild:
bash
cd
# This deletes all the previous build things
Remove-Item -Recurse -Force node_modules -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
Remove-Item -Force pnpm-lock.yaml -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
pnpm install --filter @workspace/startpage
pnpm --filter @workspace/startpage run build
Build a Specific Flavor
Each flavor lives in its own directory. For example, to build Maeger:
bash
cd Maeger
dotnet run
Or to build and publish a self-contained executable:
bash
dotnet publish -c Release -r win-x64 --self-contained true
The output will be in bin/Release/net8.0-windows/win-x64/publish/.
⌨️ Keyboard Shortcuts
Table
Shortcut	Action
Ctrl+T	New tab
Ctrl+W	Close tab
Ctrl+L	Focus address bar
Ctrl+R / F5	Reload
Ctrl+H	Home (start page)
Ctrl+Left / Ctrl+[	Back
Ctrl+Right / Ctrl+]	Forward
Ctrl+Tab / Ctrl+Shift+Tab	Next / Previous tab
F11	Full screen
Ctrl+Shift+T	Toggle terminal panel (Main / Daemon / Dev)
Ctrl+Alt+F	Toggle title bar
Ctrl+Shift+B	Toggle browser chrome
Ctrl+Shift+Alt+F	Full frameless (Zen mode)
Ctrl+Shift+S	Toggle sidebar
🎨 Features
Privacy-first — No telemetry, no accounts, no data collection. History stays on your machine.
Frameless & chrome control — Hide the title bar, the chrome, or both. Zen mode with one keystroke.
Session restore — Reopen your tabs on launch. Optional.
Integrated terminal (Main / Daemon / Dev) — Multi-tab terminal with PowerShell, CMD, WSL, and Git Bash support.
Vim-style scrolling — j/k, Ctrl+d/Ctrl+u, g/G for keyboard navigation.
Favicons on tabs — Clean, fast visual identification.
Bookmarks bar — Quick access to your saved pages.
Tab animations — Smooth entry and exit transitions.
Debug logging — Comprehensive logs written to %LocalAppData%\Yalb\logs\ for troubleshooting.
